;; PocketSurge — BIND zone file for Cloudflare DNS Import
;;
;; How to upload:
;; 1. Cloudflare Dashboard → pocketsurge.com → DNS → Records
;; 2. Import and Export → Import DNS records
;; 3. Select this file
;; 4. Leave "Proxy imported DNS records" checked (www uses cf-proxied:true)
;;
;; After import:
;; Workers & Pages → pocketsurge-landing → Domains & Routes
;; → Add Custom Domain: pocketsurge.com
;; Then add Redirect Rule: www.pocketsurge.com → https://pocketsurge.com (301)
;;
;; Apex (@) is intentionally omitted — Custom Domain creates it.

$ORIGIN pocketsurge.com.
$TTL 3600

;; www — originless placeholder so Cloudflare can apply redirect rules
www.pocketsurge.com.	3600	IN	A	192.0.2.0	; cf_tags=cf-proxied:true

;; Email hardening: this domain sends no mail (remove if you add a mailbox later)
pocketsurge.com.	3600	IN	TXT	"v=spf1 -all"
_dmarc.pocketsurge.com.	3600	IN	TXT	"v=DMARC1; p=reject; sp=reject; adkim=s; aspf=s"
